# The code defines a tuple called menu containing 5 food items (pizza, burger, pasta, salad, soup),
# then uses a for loop to print each item on its own line, preceded by a 
# "menu:" header. A tuple was used instead of a list because the menu items don't need to be modified
# — tuples are immutable, making them a good choice for fixed data.


menu = ('pizza', 'burger', 'pasta', 'salad', 'soup')

print("menu:")
for food in menu:
    print(food)